-# STO Linux Command 10.0.5
+# STO Linux Command 10.0.6
 
-A native Rust **AetherForge Dragon Glass launcher and compatibility manager for the official Arc client and Star Trek Online on Linux**. **10.0.5 hotfixes the 10.0.4 embedded-launch handshake** while preserving the AetherForge 10.0.3 OS baseline, Arc/account separation, contained STO gameplay, Visual Stability, and direct UMU + GE-Proton play.
+A native Rust **AetherForge Dragon Glass launcher and compatibility manager for the official Arc client and Star Trek Online on Linux**. **10.0.6 corrects the containment target: the official Arc client is embedded inside STO Linux Command, while PLAY STO remains a direct UMU + GE-Proton launch and is not reparented into the launcher.** The AetherForge 10.0.3 OS baseline, Visual Stability, and truthful GameClient launch confirmation remain intact.
 
 The native launcher never asks for, stores, scrapes, or logs Arc passwords, cookies, account tokens, or private authentication payloads.
 
@@ -16,6 +16,13 @@
 
 
 
+
+## v10.0.6: Embedded Arc Client + Direct STO
+
+10.0.6 fixes the containment architecture after host testing showed that the prior Gamescope/STO child-window path targeted the wrong surface. STO Linux Command now forces its own GUI onto X11/XWayland when a Wayland session exposes `DISPLAY`, launches or detects the real Arc main client, identifies Arc's X11 window by `_NET_WM_PID`/`xdotool getwindowpid` plus the Arc main-process discriminator, and reparents that Arc client window into the launcher viewport. `ArcOSBrowser.exe` is never accepted as the main Arc client.
+
+`PLAY STO` no longer participates in the containment controller. It remains Arc-independent and keeps the 10.0.5 truthful handshake: Visual Stability is prepared, the direct UMU + GE-Proton plan is launched through Gamescope for frame pacing, and the activity stays waiting until `GameClient.exe` is observed. The STO sign-in/launcher/game surface is not embedded in STO Linux Command.
+
 ## v10.0.5: Arc/STO Launch Handshake Hotfix
 
 10.0.5 fixes three runtime-state defects found after the first 10.0.4 host launch: Arc browser helpers no longer count as the Arc main client, STO launcher discovery rejects Arc-side stubs and prefers the real Star Trek Online game tree, and Gamescope startup no longer counts as a completed STO launch. The launch activity remains waiting until `GameClient.exe` is observed, and failures preserve the detected launcher path, Gamescope PID, and `sto-launch.log` location for diagnosis.
diff -ruN a/crates/sto-gui/src/embedded_arc.rs b/crates/sto-gui/src/embedded_arc.rs
--- a/crates/sto-gui/src/embedded_arc.rs	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/crates/sto-gui/src/embedded_arc.rs	2026-09-19 00:48:47.554659219 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,371 @@
+use crate::arc_bridge;
+use std::{
+    env, fs,
+    path::{Path, PathBuf},
+    process::Command,
+    time::{Duration, Instant},
+};
+
+const ATTACH_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(25);
+const X11_HOST_MARKER: &str = "AETHERFORGE_STO_X11_HOST";
+
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct ViewportRect {
+    pub x: i32,
+    pub y: i32,
+    pub width: u32,
+    pub height: u32,
+}
+
+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
+pub struct ArcEmbedPrerequisites {
+    pub xdotool: PathBuf,
+    pub display: String,
+}
+
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub enum ArcEmbedEvent {
+    None,
+    Attached,
+    Exited,
+    Failed(String),
+}
+
+#[derive(Debug, Default)]
+pub struct EmbeddedArcController {
+    host_pid: Option<u32>,
+    launcher_window: Option<String>,
+    child_window: Option<String>,
+    pending_since: Option<Instant>,
+    last_rect: Option<ViewportRect>,
+    error: Option<String>,
+}
+
+impl EmbeddedArcController {
+    pub fn begin_pending(&mut self, host_pid: Option<u32>) {
+        self.host_pid = host_pid;
+        self.launcher_window = None;
+        self.child_window = None;
+        self.pending_since = Some(Instant::now());
+        self.last_rect = None;
+        self.error = None;
+    }
+
+    pub fn is_running_or_pending(&self) -> bool {
+        self.pending_since.is_some() || self.child_window.is_some()
+    }
+
+    pub fn is_attached(&self) -> bool {
+        self.child_window.is_some()
+    }
+
+    pub fn error(&self) -> Option<&str> {
+        self.error.as_deref()
+    }
+
+    pub fn poll(&mut self, xdotool: &Path) -> ArcEmbedEvent {
+        if let Some(child) = self.child_window.clone() {
+            if window_exists(xdotool, &child) {
+                return ArcEmbedEvent::None;
+            }
+            self.child_window = None;
+            self.last_rect = None;
+            self.pending_since = Some(Instant::now());
+        }
+
+        if !arc_bridge::detect_arc_process() {
+            if self.host_pid.is_some_and(|pid| !process_exists(pid)) {
+                self.reset();
+                return ArcEmbedEvent::Exited;
+            }
+            if self.pending_since.is_some_and(|started| started.elapsed() >= ATTACH_TIMEOUT) {
+                let message = "Arc was started, but the Arc main client did not become available for containment.".to_string();
+                self.fail_containment(message.clone());
+                return ArcEmbedEvent::Failed(message);
+            }
+            return ArcEmbedEvent::None;
+        }
+
+        match self.try_attach(xdotool) {
+            Ok(true) => ArcEmbedEvent::Attached,
+            Ok(false) => {
+                if self.pending_since.is_some_and(|started| started.elapsed() >= ATTACH_TIMEOUT) {
+                    let message = "Arc is running, but its X11/XWayland client window could not be attached inside STO Linux Command.".to_string();
+                    self.fail_containment(message.clone());
+                    ArcEmbedEvent::Failed(message)
+                } else {
+                    ArcEmbedEvent::None
+                }
+            }
+            Err(error) => {
+                if self.pending_since.is_some_and(|started| started.elapsed() >= ATTACH_TIMEOUT) {
+                    let message = format!("Arc containment failed: {error}");
+                    self.fail_containment(message.clone());
+                    ArcEmbedEvent::Failed(message)
+                } else {
+                    ArcEmbedEvent::None
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    pub fn sync_rect(&mut self, xdotool: &Path, rect: ViewportRect) -> Result<(), String> {
+        let Some(child) = self.child_window.as_deref() else {
+            return Ok(());
+        };
+        if self.last_rect == Some(rect) {
+            return Ok(());
+        }
+        run_xdotool(
+            xdotool,
+            &["windowmove", "--sync", child, &rect.x.to_string(), &rect.y.to_string()],
+        )?;
+        run_xdotool(
+            xdotool,
+            &["windowsize", "--sync", child, &rect.width.to_string(), &rect.height.to_string()],
+        )?;
+        self.last_rect = Some(rect);
+        Ok(())
+    }
+
+    pub fn focus_arc(&self, xdotool: &Path) -> Result<(), String> {
+        let child = self
+            .child_window
+            .as_deref()
+            .ok_or_else(|| "Arc viewport is not attached yet".to_string())?;
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowfocus", "--sync", child])?;
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowraise", child])
+    }
+
+    pub fn release_focus(&self, xdotool: &Path) -> Result<(), String> {
+        let launcher = self
+            .launcher_window
+            .as_deref()
+            .ok_or_else(|| "launcher X11 window is not known yet".to_string())?;
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowfocus", "--sync", launcher])
+    }
+
+    pub fn terminate(&mut self) {
+        if let Some(child) = self.child_window.as_deref() {
+            if let Some(xdotool) = find_program("xdotool") {
+                let _ = run_xdotool(&xdotool, &["windowclose", child]);
+            }
+        }
+        if let Some(pid) = self.host_pid {
+            let process_group = format!("-{pid}");
+            let _ = Command::new("kill")
+                .args(["-TERM", "--", &process_group])
+                .status();
+        }
+        self.reset();
+    }
+
+    fn try_attach(&mut self, xdotool: &Path) -> Result<bool, String> {
+        let launcher = match self.launcher_window.clone() {
+            Some(window) => window,
+            None => {
+                let windows = search_windows(
+                    xdotool,
+                    &["search", "--onlyvisible", "--pid", &std::process::id().to_string(), ".*"],
+                )?;
+                let Some(window) = windows.into_iter().next() else {
+                    return Ok(false);
+                };
+                self.launcher_window = Some(window.clone());
+                window
+            }
+        };
+
+        let Some(child) = find_arc_main_window(xdotool, &launcher)? else {
+            return Ok(false);
+        };
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowreparent", &child, &launcher])?;
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowraise", &child])?;
+        self.child_window = Some(child);
+        self.last_rect = None;
+        Ok(true)
+    }
+
+    fn fail_containment(&mut self, message: String) {
+        // Only terminate a process group that this launcher started. An Arc
+        // process that was already running before the request is left alone.
+        if let Some(pid) = self.host_pid {
+            let process_group = format!("-{pid}");
+            let _ = Command::new("kill")
+                .args(["-TERM", "--", &process_group])
+                .status();
+        }
+        self.host_pid = None;
+        self.child_window = None;
+        self.launcher_window = None;
+        self.pending_since = None;
+        self.last_rect = None;
+        self.error = Some(message);
+    }
+
+    fn reset(&mut self) {
+        self.host_pid = None;
+        self.launcher_window = None;
+        self.child_window = None;
+        self.pending_since = None;
+        self.last_rect = None;
+        self.error = None;
+    }
+}
+
+pub fn detect_prerequisites() -> Result<ArcEmbedPrerequisites, String> {
+    let display = env::var("DISPLAY").map_err(|_| {
+        "Embedded Arc requires X11/XWayland. XWayland must be installed and DISPLAY must be available.".to_string()
+    })?;
+    if display.trim().is_empty() {
+        return Err("Embedded Arc requires a non-empty X11/XWayland DISPLAY".into());
+    }
+    let xdotool = find_program("xdotool").ok_or_else(|| {
+        "xdotool is required to embed Arc inside STO Linux Command. On Arch: sudo pacman -S --needed xdotool".to_string()
+    })?;
+    Ok(ArcEmbedPrerequisites { xdotool, display })
+}
+
+pub fn ensure_launcher_x11_backend() -> Result<(), String> {
+    let wayland_present = env::var_os("WAYLAND_DISPLAY").is_some() || env::var_os("WAYLAND_SOCKET").is_some();
+    if !wayland_present {
+        return Ok(());
+    }
+    if env::var_os("DISPLAY").is_none() {
+        return Err("Arc containment requires XWayland, but DISPLAY is unavailable".into());
+    }
+    if env::var_os(X11_HOST_MARKER).is_some() {
+        return Ok(());
+    }
+
+    let exe = env::current_exe().map_err(|error| format!("locate STO Linux Command executable: {error}"))?;
+    let mut command = Command::new(exe);
+    command.args(env::args_os().skip(1));
+    command.env_remove("WAYLAND_DISPLAY");
+    command.env_remove("WAYLAND_SOCKET");
+    command.env(X11_HOST_MARKER, "1");
+
+    #[cfg(unix)]
+    {
+        use std::os::unix::process::CommandExt;
+        let error = command.exec();
+        return Err(format!("re-exec STO Linux Command on X11/XWayland failed: {error}"));
+    }
+    #[allow(unreachable_code)]
+    Err("Arc containment requires a Unix X11/XWayland host".into())
+}
+
+fn find_arc_main_window(xdotool: &Path, launcher_window: &str) -> Result<Option<String>, String> {
+    let windows = search_windows(xdotool, &["search", "--onlyvisible", "--name", ".*"])?;
+    let mut identity_fallback = None;
+    for window in windows {
+        if window == launcher_window {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if let Some(pid) = window_pid(xdotool, &window)? {
+            if let Some(cmdline) = process_cmdline(pid) {
+                if arc_bridge::matches_arc_main_process(&cmdline) {
+                    return Ok(Some(window));
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        let title = window_property(xdotool, "getwindowname", &window)?.unwrap_or_default();
+        let class = window_property(xdotool, "getwindowclassname", &window)?.unwrap_or_default();
+        if identity_fallback.is_none() && looks_like_arc_window_identity(&title, &class) {
+            identity_fallback = Some(window);
+        }
+    }
+    Ok(identity_fallback)
+}
+
+fn looks_like_arc_window_identity(title: &str, class: &str) -> bool {
+    let identity = format!("{title} {class}").to_ascii_lowercase();
+    identity.contains("arc")
+        && !identity.contains("aetherforge")
+        && !identity.contains("arcosbrowser")
+        && !identity.contains("chromium")
+        && !identity.contains("cef")
+        && !identity.contains("star trek online")
+}
+
+
+fn window_property(xdotool: &Path, command: &str, window: &str) -> Result<Option<String>, String> {
+    let output = Command::new(xdotool)
+        .args([command, window])
+        .output()
+        .map_err(|error| format!("failed to query Arc window identity: {error}"))?;
+    if !output.status.success() {
+        return Ok(None);
+    }
+    let value = String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout).trim().to_string();
+    Ok((!value.is_empty()).then_some(value))
+}
+
+fn window_pid(xdotool: &Path, window: &str) -> Result<Option<u32>, String> {
+    let output = Command::new(xdotool)
+        .args(["getwindowpid", window])
+        .output()
+        .map_err(|error| format!("failed to query Arc window PID: {error}"))?;
+    if !output.status.success() {
+        return Ok(None);
+    }
+    Ok(String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout).trim().parse().ok())
+}
+
+fn process_cmdline(pid: u32) -> Option<String> {
+    let bytes = fs::read(Path::new("/proc").join(pid.to_string()).join("cmdline")).ok()?;
+    if bytes.is_empty() {
+        return None;
+    }
+    Some(String::from_utf8_lossy(&bytes).replace('\0', " "))
+}
+
+fn process_exists(pid: u32) -> bool {
+    Path::new("/proc").join(pid.to_string()).exists()
+}
+
+fn window_exists(xdotool: &Path, window: &str) -> bool {
+    Command::new(xdotool)
+        .args(["getwindowname", window])
+        .output()
+        .is_ok_and(|output| output.status.success())
+}
+
+fn find_program(name: &str) -> Option<PathBuf> {
+    let path = env::var_os("PATH")?;
+    env::split_paths(&path)
+        .map(|dir| dir.join(name))
+        .find(|candidate| candidate.is_file())
+}
+
+fn search_windows(xdotool: &Path, args: &[&str]) -> Result<Vec<String>, String> {
+    let output = Command::new(xdotool)
+        .args(args)
+        .output()
+        .map_err(|error| format!("failed to run {}: {error}", xdotool.display()))?;
+    if !output.status.success() {
+        return Ok(Vec::new());
+    }
+    Ok(String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout)
+        .lines()
+        .map(str::trim)
+        .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
+        .map(str::to_string)
+        .collect())
+}
+
+fn run_xdotool(xdotool: &Path, args: &[&str]) -> Result<(), String> {
+    let output = Command::new(xdotool)
+        .args(args)
+        .output()
+        .map_err(|error| format!("failed to run {}: {error}", xdotool.display()))?;
+    if output.status.success() {
+        return Ok(());
+    }
+    Err(format!(
+        "{} {} failed: {}",
+        xdotool.display(),
+        args.join(" "),
+        String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stderr).trim()
+    ))
+}
